From 0642c075d0dc134dcf95a020f134bc80538a1f36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:06:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Decide each release's storage actions in SQL, and a
 selection's by their least

Rust derived what a release offers (upload, pin, unpin, move to this
device) from its rows and the sync status, and the Storage Manager's
selection intersected those lists in Rust. Each action is now a column of
the statement that reads the release, the selection offers an action when
every selected row does (the least of each column) and only cancelling
when one is moving or failed (the greatest of one flag), and the Mac
menu acts on the rows core answered for the selection it shows instead of
filtering its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019wwAR8vet2nCM1HhYR5VRz
